      "page_title": "Diagnosing Plans: Signatures & Scans",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Three Steps",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              "biggest time x loops",
              "rows vs actual",
              "read BUFFERS",
              "fix"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Find the node with largest actual time x loops, not largest cost",
            "Check that node's estimate against its actual",
            "`shared read` went to disk, `shared hit` came from cache"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Inclusive Time",
          "text": "A node's `actual time` INCLUDES all its children. Subtract the children to get self-time."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Signatures",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Symptom",
            "Diagnosis"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`loops=48000`",
              "48000 x 0.03ms = 1.4s hidden"
            ],
            [
              "`Rows Removed by Filter: 4900000`",
              "index the filtered column"
            ],
            [
              "`external merge Disk: 180MB`",
              "raise work_mem or index the order"
            ],
            [
              "`Batches: 16`",
              "build side underestimated"
            ],
            [
              "`Heap Fetches: 890000`",
              "VACUUM to refresh the VM"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "text",
          "lines": [
            "-> Index Scan on orders",
            "     (actual time=0.02..0.03 rows=1 loops=48000)",
            "-- per-loop time looks trivial; total is not"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`Workers Planned: 4 Workers Launched: 0` — pool exhausted",
            "`Rows Removed by Join Filter` — non-equi condition after the join",
            "`Rows Removed by Index Recheck` — lossy bitmap pages burning CPU"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Visualizers",
          "items": [
            "`explain.depesz.com` colours estimate drift",
            "`explain.dalibo.com` gives a tree view",
            "Both highlight mismatches automatically"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "BUFFERS First",
          "text": "Millions of `shared read` blocks means the data is not cached — no plan change fixes cold IO."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Scan Comparison",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Scan",
            "Cost shape",
            "IO"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Seq",
              "O(pages)",
              "sequential"
            ],
            [
              "Index",
              "O(log n + k)",
              "random"
            ],
            [
              "Bitmap",
              "index + heap",
              "page order"
            ],
            [
              "Index Only",
              "index alone",
              "no heap"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Merge is near free when both sides are pre-sorted",
            "Index Only Scan is the only scan that skips the heap",
            "Worth designing schemas and indexes around"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "sql",
          "lines": [
            "CREATE INDEX act_ord ON orders (created_at)",
            "  WHERE status = 'active';  -- partial"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Join Costs & Index Economics",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Not In Node Times",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Trigger time is reported separately after the plan",
            "It is not included in any node's actual time",
            "Always run the query twice",
            "First run is cold cache, second run is the plan"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "qa",
          "q": "Huge cost node, tiny actual time. Chase it?",
          "a_bullets": [
            "No — cost is an estimate, not a measurement",
            "Rank nodes by actual time x loops instead",
            "Only then check whether its estimate broke"
          ],
          "example_code": [
            "Hash Join (cost=98000..120000 rows=12)",
            "           (actual time=1.1..1.3 rows=11 loops=1)"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Join Comparison",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Join",
            "Complexity",
            "Memory"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Nested Loop",
              "O(N x M)",
              "none"
            ],
            [
              "Nested Loop idx",
              "O(N log M)",
              "none"
            ],
            [
              "Hash",
              "O(N + M)",
              "work_mem"
            ],
            [
              "Merge",
              "O(N log N + M log M)",
              "low"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Hash Needs Equality",
          "text": "Hash Join supports only `=`. A `<` or `>` join condition falls back to Nested Loop — watch `Join Filter`."
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Memoize Node",
          "items": [
            "Caches ==inner results== across loops",
            "Pays off when join keys **repeat**",
            "Turns a repeated probe into a lookup"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Index Economics",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Every index speeds reads, taxes INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE",
            "It also lengthens every VACUUM",
            "Composite order: equality, then range, then ORDER BY",
            "Partial index can be a fraction of the size",
            "Small index stays hot in cache"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Tuning Levers & Query Rewrites",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Config Levers"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Knob",
            "Move"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`random_page_cost`",
              "4.0 to 1.1 on SSD"
            ],
            [
              "`effective_cache_size`",
              "50-75% of RAM, allocates nothing"
            ],
            [
              "`work_mem`",
              "low = disk sorts, high = OOM"
            ],
            [
              "`default_statistics_target`",
              "100 to 500 on skewed cols"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`random_page_cost` on SSD is the highest-leverage change",
            "work_mem risk is connections times nodes multiplying",
            "Higher statistics target costs ANALYZE time, buys accuracy"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Rewrites That Unlock Plans"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "EXISTS instead of IN on large subqueries",
            "LATERAL instead of a correlated scalar subquery",
            "Never wrap the indexed column in a function",
            "Keyset `WHERE id > last_id` instead of `OFFSET N`"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "OFFSET Tax",
          "text": "`OFFSET 100000` scans and discards 100,000 rows every page. Keyset pagination stays constant time."
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "When No Plan Is Enough",
          "items": [
            "Denormalize, or add a materialized view",
            "Refresh cost is the trade you accept",
            "Partitioning helps only if the key is in WHERE",
            "Otherwise every partition is scanned"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Where vs Why",
          "text": "`pg_stat_statements` tells you WHICH query to EXPLAIN. EXPLAIN tells you why it is slow."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Standard Invocation",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "sql",
          "lines": [
            "EXPLAIN (ANALYZE, BUFFERS, VERBOSE,",
            "         SETTINGS, FORMAT TEXT)",
            "SELECT ... ;"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "The Whole Discipline",
          "text": "Find the node where estimated rows and actual rows diverge most. Everything after that is follow-up."
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Cost is the planner's opinion, actual time is the truth",
            "`EXPLAIN` alone shows only the opinion",
            "Actual time and rows are per-loop — always multiply"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Triage Order",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              "pg_stat_statements",
              "EXPLAIN ANALYZE BUFFERS",
              "pg_stats",
              "fix"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Fix Ladder, Flags & Diagnostic Toggles",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Fix Ladder, Cheapest First",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "ANALYZE the table",
            "Extended statistics on correlated columns",
            "Raise the per-column statistics target",
            "Add an index, then rewrite the query",
            "Config change, and only then a hint"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Never Ship Flashlights",
          "text": "An `enable_*` setting left off in production is a debugging tool you forgot to put down."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Cheat Sheets"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Rows matched",
            "Scan"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "under 1%",
              "Index"
            ],
            [
              "1-10%",
              "Bitmap"
            ],
            [
              "over 10%",
              "Seq"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Shape",
            "Join"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "tiny outer + indexed inner",
              "Nested Loop"
            ],
            [
              "big equality",
              "Hash"
            ],
            [
              "both sorted",
              "Merge"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Red Flag List",
          "items": [
            "`Batches` over 1, `Sort Method: external`",
            "Lossy `Heap Blocks`, high `Heap Fetches`",
            "`Rows Removed by Filter` in the millions",
            "`loops` in the thousands"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Flags Worth Adding",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Flag",
            "Adds"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "BUFFERS",
              "hit/read counts"
            ],
            [
              "VERBOSE",
              "output columns"
            ],
            [
              "SETTINGS",
              "changed GUCs"
            ],
            [
              "TIMING OFF",
              "less overhead"
            ],
            [
              "FORMAT JSON",
              "machine parsing"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`BUFFERS` is the single most useful extra flag",
            "`TIMING OFF` when gettimeofday distorts a fast query",
            "`Planning Time` above `Execution Time` means planning is the cost"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Diagnostic Flashlights",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "sql",
          "lines": [
            "SET enable_nestloop = off;  -- prove it",
            "EXPLAIN ANALYZE SELECT ... ;",
            "RESET enable_nestloop;"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Toggles prove which plan you wanted, they never fix it",
            "`pg_hint_plan` for real hints when nothing else lands",
            "`join_collapse_limit` 8 caps exhaustive join-order search"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "qa",
          "q": "ANALYZE ran, estimate still 100x low. Next?",
          "a_bullets": [
            "Columns are correlated — independence assumption lies",
            "Add extended statistics on the pair",
            "Re-ANALYZE, then re-read the node"
          ],
          "example_code": [
            "CREATE STATISTICS s (dependencies, mcv)",
            "  ON city, state FROM addr;"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Stats Are The Cheap Win",
          "text": "`ALTER TABLE t ALTER COLUMN c SET STATISTICS 1000;` then re-ANALYZE — cheaper than any new index."
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "sql",
          "lines": [
            "BEGIN;",
            "EXPLAIN ANALYZE DELETE FROM t WHERE id < 100;",
            "ROLLBACK;  -- safe on INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Missing Stats & Default Planner Guesses",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "When Stats Are Missing",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Case",
            "Planner guess"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "equality",
              "0.5%"
            ],
            [
              "range",
              "33%"
            ],
            [
              "fresh restore",
              "nothing"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Check `last_analyze` in `pg_stat_user_tables` first",
            "Expression indexes carry their own statistics",
            "A bare `lower(email)` filter falls back to the default guess"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Index Types, Stats Freshness & Memory Spills",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Loops Reminder",
          "items": [
            "`actual rows` and `actual time` are per loop",
            "Multiply by `loops` for the real total",
            "Parallel node rows are per worker too"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Before You Benchmark"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "ANALYZE after every bulk load, restore, or data shift",
            "Test on production-sized data",
            "A plan right for 1,000 rows is wrong for 10,000,000",
            "`auto_explain` with `log_min_duration` catches the rest"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Index Type Picker",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Type",
            "Use for"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "B-tree",
              "=, <, >, BETWEEN, prefix LIKE"
            ],
            [
              "GIN",
              "arrays, full text"
            ],
            [
              "GiST",
              "ranges, geometry"
            ],
            [
              "BRIN",
              "huge ordered tables"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "sql",
          "lines": [
            "CREATE INDEX o_cust ON orders",
            "  (customer_id, created_at)",
            "  INCLUDE (total);  -- covering"
          ],
          "note": "Index Only Scan needs fresh VM"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Stats Freshness",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "sql",
          "lines": [
            "SELECT relname, last_analyze,",
            "       last_autoanalyze",
            "FROM pg_stat_user_tables",
            "ORDER BY last_autoanalyze;"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Autovacuum analyzes after ==50 + 10%== of rows change",
            "On huge tables that threshold drifts for **days**",
            "Bulk load or restore — run ANALYZE by hand"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Memory Spill Signs",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Node",
            "Spill signal"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Sort",
              "`external merge Disk`"
            ],
            [
              "Hash",
              "`Batches` over 1"
            ],
            [
              "HashAggregate",
              "`Disk Usage`"
            ],
            [
              "Bitmap Heap",
              "`lossy` blocks"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "work_mem Multiplies",
          "text": "It is granted per sort or hash node, per worker. Raise it per session, not globally."
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "cloud",
          "title": "Not Your Adversary",
          "text": "The planner is a cost model running on statistics. Give it better statistics and it makes better choices."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Parallel Scan Gates & Setup Costs",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. The Gate",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Parallelism is not automatic. The table must be large enough to justify the overhead of spawning workers.",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Default threshold is **8MB**",
            "Check `pg_class.reltuples` x `avg_width`",
            "Small tables always use sequential scan"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "sql",
          "lines": [
            "SELECT relname, reltuples * avg_width",
            "FROM pg_class c JOIN pg_stats s",
            "WHERE relname = 'orders';"
          ],
          "note": "Estimate size in bytes"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. The Setting",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Parameter",
            "Default",
            "Effect"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`min_parallel_table_scan_size`",
              "8MB",
              "Min table size"
            ],
            [
              "`min_parallel_index_scan_size`",
              "512kB",
              "Min index size"
            ],
            [
              "`max_parallel_workers_per_gather`",
              "2",
              "Max workers"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Lowering it forces parallelism on small data",
            "Raising it prevents overhead on medium data",
            "Index scans have their own separate threshold"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "sql",
          "lines": [
            "SET min_parallel_table_scan_size",
            "    TO 0;  -- test only",
            "EXPLAIN ANALYZE",
            "SELECT count(*) FROM orders;",
            "RESET ALL;"
          ],
          "note": "session-scoped; never set globally"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "sticky",
          "title": "Cluster Caps",
          "text": "`max_parallel_workers` (8) and `max_worker_processes` (8) cap the whole cluster, not one query."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Why It Exists",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Cost",
            "Default",
            "Charges"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`parallel_setup_cost`",
              "1000",
              "worker launch"
            ],
            [
              "`parallel_tuple_cost`",
              "0.1",
              "each row to leader"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "The 8MB Rule",
          "text": "If your table is under 8MB, parallelism will likely make it **slower**, not faster."
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Key Takeaway",
          "text": "Tables must exceed **8MB** before parallelism is considered. Check your table size first."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Reading Gather Nodes & Worker Rows",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Small queries never earn back the ==1000== setup",
            "Every row through Gather pays **0.1** extra",
            "Aggregating before Gather keeps transfer tiny"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "text",
          "lines": [
            "Gather (actual rows=3 loops=1)",
            "  Workers Planned: 2",
            "  Workers Launched: 2",
            "  -> Partial Aggregate",
            "    -> Parallel Seq Scan"
          ],
          "note": "3 rows cross, not millions"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`Launched` below `Planned` — pool ran out",
            "Leader also scans unless it is busy gathering",
            "Fewer workers than planned still returns correct rows"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Overhead Costs",
          "items": [
            "Worker startup takes milliseconds",
            "Memory allocation per worker",
            "Synchronization barriers between nodes",
            "Network traffic if distributed"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Checking Your Table",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "sql",
          "lines": [
            "SELECT pg_size_pretty(pg_total_relation_size('orders'));",
            "-- Compare against 8MB threshold",
            "-- If smaller, parallelism is disabled"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Use `pg_total_relation_size` for accurate size",
            "Includes indexes and TOAST data",
            "Compare against `min_parallel_table_scan_size`"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Common Mistakes",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Assuming parallelism is always beneficial",
            "Ignoring the 8MB minimum threshold",
            "Forcing parallelism on small tables",
            "Not checking `pg_class` for actual size"
          ],
          "style": "cross"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "6. Per-Worker Rows",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "text",
          "lines": [
            "-> Parallel Seq Scan on orders",
            "   (actual rows=333333 loops=3)",
            "-- 333333 x 3 = ~1M rows"
          ],
          "note": "loops = leader + 2 workers"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Parallel node rows are ==per process==",
            "Multiply by `loops` for the true total",
            "Uneven splits show up as skewed worker rows"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "7. Order and Memory",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Node",
            "Behavior"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Gather",
              "order **lost**"
            ],
            [
              "Gather Merge",
              "sort preserved"
            ],
            [
              "each worker",
              "own `work_mem`"
            ]
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
